  "question": {
    "text": "A variable circle passes through the fixed point $A(p, q)$ and touches $x$-axis. The locus of the other end of the diameter through $\\mathrm{A}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kEb9d",
      "text": "\n$(x-p)^2=4 q y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "yBH9Y",
      "text": "\n$(x-q)^2=4 p y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "liSZy",
      "text": "\n$(y-p)^2=4 q x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cdLAP",
      "text": "\n$(y-q)^2=4 p x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the other end of diameter is $(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})$ then equation of circle is\n$$\n(x-h)(x-p)+(y-k)(y-q)=0\n$$\nPut $y=0$, since $x$-axis touches the circle\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow x^2-(h+p) x+(h p+k q)=0 \\Rightarrow(h+p)^2=4(h p+k q) \\quad(D=0) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(x-p)^2=4 q y .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
